    relevance: "Collections are Java's data structures with contracts: List keeps order and duplicates, Set enforces uniqueness, Map looks up by key. Declaring by the INTERFACE (List<String> queue = new ArrayList<>()) keeps the choice swappable — and picking the structure whose contract matches the question is the same skill as Python's collections lesson.",
