    relevance: "The Java block's payoff, mirroring the Python track's: most Java vulnerabilities are input and output failures — unvalidated values reaching queries, comparisons that leak timing, raw user text rendered as markup. These three habits (validate in layers, compare in constant time, escape/parameterise at boundaries) are the reviewed standard.",
