      "Secret comparison: String.equals short-circuits at the first different character — a timing side channel. MessageDigest.isEqual(a, b) compares ALL bytes in constant time and is the standard for tokens, MACs, and password-derived values — the same lesson as Python's compare_digest, in the Java API.",
      "Output is context: user text rendered into HTML must be escaped (< becomes &lt;) or it becomes markup (XSS); user values entering SQL must go through PreparedStatement parameters (the driver binds them as DATA, never as query text — SQL injection's structural fix). The demo escapes for display; the rule for SQL is stated and non-negotiable: parameterise, never concatenate.",
