    code: { lang: "java", title: "SecurityDemo.java — complete, runnable (Java 17)", code: "import java.security.MessageDigest;\n\npublic class SecurityDemo {\n    static boolean validPort(String text) {          // one gate, three layers\n        try {\n            int p = Integer.parseInt(text);          // layer 1: strict parse\n            return p >= 1 && p <= 65535;             // layer 2: range\n        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {\n            return false;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(\"443 valid? \" + validPort(\"443\"));\n        System.out.println(\"70000 valid? \" + validPort(\"70000\"));\n        System.out.println(\"'443; DROP' valid? \" + validPort(\"443; DROP\"));\n\n        byte[] a = \"expected-token\".getBytes();\n        byte[] b = \"expected-token\".getBytes();\n        byte[] c = \"attacker-token\".getBytes();\n        System.out.println(\"constant-time equal (same): \" + MessageDigest.isEqual(a, b));\n        System.out.println(\"constant-time equal (diff): \" + MessageDigest.isEqual(a, c));\n\n        String userInput = \"<script>alert(1)</script>\";\n        String safe = userInput.replace(\"<\", \"&lt;\").replace(\">\", \"&gt;\");\n        System.out.println(\"escaped for display: \" + safe);\n    }\n}", output: "443 valid? true\n70000 valid? false\n'443; DROP' valid? false\nconstant-time equal (same): true\nconstant-time equal (diff): false\nescaped for display: &lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;", lines: ["'443; DROP' dies at layer 1: parseInt refuses the WHOLE string — strict parsing is the injection defence at this gate.", "70000 parses cleanly and dies at layer 2 — the layers catch different failure classes.", "isEqual compares every byte: same tokens true, different false, and the TIMING reveals nothing about where they differ.", "The escaped output displays as text in a browser — &lt; is data, < would have been markup."] },
    mistakes: ["Validating with contains(\"443\") or regex fragments — partial matches let '443; DROP' through; strict parse is the gate.", "Comparing tokens with .equals — timing leaks position information.", "Building SQL or HTML by concatenating raw input — injection in both contexts, one habit."],
    security: "This lesson is the Java form of the level's thesis: validate in layers at input, parameterise/escape at output, compare secrets in constant time. CWE-89 (SQL injection), CWE-79 (XSS), and CWE-208 (timing) are the classes these habits retire.",
    pc: ["Run SecurityDemo.java; add a layer-3 allowlist (only 22, 80, 443, 3389 pass) and predict the three verdicts again.", "Find the PreparedStatement pattern in the Java docs and write the two-line shape (query with ?, setString) from memory."],
    android: ["Android: WebView rendering and SQLite queries are exactly these two boundaries — escape and parameterise."],
    lab: "Guided lab: in the Playground, write validHost(String) that accepts only letters, digits, dots, and hyphens (an allowlist loop) and test it on 'lab-web', 'a b', and 'x;rm'.",
